Dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rust crates and npm packages keep their own licences. The packages shipped in
deb/RPM/Flatpak get a generated bundle at
`/usr/share/doc/easy-edits-pro/third-party-notices/` — readable
`NOTICE-DEPENDENCIES.md`, a machine-readable `inventory.json` and verbatim
copies of every-dependency licence text. It is regenerated by
`scripts/generate-notice-bundle.py` at package build time from the Cargo
lockfiles, the pnpm production closure and the repository-tracked texts
(`licenses/`, `assets/fonts/`); never edit its output by hand. System
libraries such as GStreamer are loaded dynamically from the user's system
(deb Depends / RPM Requires) except for GES, which the Flatpak builds from
its pinned upstream source archive. Packages whose upstream archive carries
no licence file receive the canonical SPDX identifier text for their declared
licence from `licenses/third-party/canonical/` (see the next entry). Known
gaps (e.g. version-matched ONNX Runtime notices) are carried into that
bundle's `UNRESOLVED` list until real evidence lands.

Canonical SPDX identifier texts (licenses/third-party/canonical/)
  Standard SPDX license-list texts for the identifiers that some upstream
  crates ship no file for, downloaded from
  https://spdx.org/licenses/ (free redistribution, no copyright asserted by
  SPDX). So that generated notices name exactly the right text for a
  declared licence identifier even when the upstream archive omits one.

Hosted plugin support (Packet 4.1) embeds the
[Clack](https://github.com/enzo1981/clack) suite (crates `clack-host`,
`clack-plugin`, `clack-common`, `clack-extensions`,
Licence: MIT OR Apache-2.0, texts generated by the crates' own licence terms).
EEP links `clack-host` as the CLAP plugin host for `saturn-audio-dsp`; no
Clack source code is copied into EEP.

